# Female lower-LOD left-hand retention

This private delivery retains the existing LOD0 left-hand surface in Scout and Shawl LOD1/2. It adds no materials, textures, joints, or draw calls. The frozen thumb motion is unchanged.

Apply only `source.patch` and `test.patch`; do not copy the complete optimizer over concurrent collar changes. Copy only the four files in `models/` after checking their original hashes in `proof/body-records.json`. Update those four appearance LOD records in the current canonical manifest. Do not copy a private manifest or animation bank.

All 54 exported checks pass at 120 Hz. The regression expands to all three LODs and both hands on Granadero, Scout, and Shawl. It keeps zero crossings, the connected-web area bound, and actual thumb-shaft angle bound.

Every non-left-hand triangle is exact, including named native weights, normals, UVs, pigments, and all cloth morph positions/normals. Raw non-Skin accessor payloads and native rest matrices are exact. Materials, samplers, image bindings, and external texture bytes are exact.

The source build correctly reproduces the retained hand. A separate full-rebuild drift changes old Shawl cloth morphs even without this optimizer patch. To exclude that unrelated drift, the delivery composes only the source-built Skin primitive into each existing body, with exact non-left Skin triangle proof. `proof/compose-hand-only.py` records this deterministic step.

The loose thumb extension and sharp inner index crease remain. This does not claim complete hand anatomy. See `receipt.json` for hashes, costs, evidence, limits, and integration instructions.
